  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Angel Support Programme (Nigeria)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen the organisational capacity of the Lagos Angel Network (LAN), one of Nigeria&apos;s most prominent Business Angel Network. It will do so through providing training and onboarding 40 new angel investors.This project thereby contributes to a supportive environment for young entrepreneurs, given that angel investors play a crucial role in empowering aspiring entrepreneurs, offering financial support, expertise and networks.By collaborating with the African Angel Academy (AAA), a pan-African investor education platform currently led by Viktoria Ventures, AAA will deliver high-quality training and support LAN in standardising their angel onboarding process. This will increase the knowledge of newly onboarded angels, boost investor confidence, improve deal quality, and encourage more local capital to stay in the country and flow into early-stage enterprises, including those coming from the Orange Corners programme.</narrative>
  </description>
